# Huawei VSA dictionary subset — radstorm (vendor-id 2011)
#
# Purpose: Maps the Huawei vendor-specific attributes radstorm cares
# about (see docs/PROTOCOL.md) to human-readable names. Sourced from
# FreeRADIUS' dictionary.huawei. This is a curated subset — full Huawei
# dictionary is not needed for radstorm's CoA/Disconnect handling.
#
# Related: pkg/radius/dictionary.go, pkg/radius/vendor.go, docs/PROTOCOL.md
# Briefing: .orchestration/briefings/1a-radius-protocol.md
# Contract: Vendor-Type IDs are fixed by Huawei; names should follow the
# Huawei- prefix convention.
#
# Format: VENDOR <name> <id>
#         VENDOR-ATTRIBUTE <vendor-name> <attr-name> <vendor-type> <type>

VENDOR Huawei 2011

VENDOR-ATTRIBUTE Huawei Huawei-Input-Peak-Rate         1   integer
VENDOR-ATTRIBUTE Huawei Huawei-Input-Average-Rate      2   integer
VENDOR-ATTRIBUTE Huawei Huawei-Input-Basic-Rate        3   integer
VENDOR-ATTRIBUTE Huawei Huawei-Output-Peak-Rate        5   integer
VENDOR-ATTRIBUTE Huawei Huawei-Output-Average-Rate     6   integer
VENDOR-ATTRIBUTE Huawei Huawei-Output-Basic-Rate       7   integer
VENDOR-ATTRIBUTE Huawei Huawei-Subscriber-QoS-Profile  18  string
VENDOR-ATTRIBUTE Huawei Huawei-Connect-Id              20  integer
VENDOR-ATTRIBUTE Huawei Huawei-Acct-Session-Id         26  string
VENDOR-ATTRIBUTE Huawei Huawei-Service-Type            65  integer
